Hi,

Has anyone seen the following problem? :

I installed kernel 2.4.27 with ACPI, and everything goes fine until I start
KDE. While KDE is starting, the computer spontaneously reboots, and I have
to sit through a long fsck of all the uncleanly mounted filesystems.

There's no way I can get into KDE without the computer spontaneously hanging
and rebooting. 

Any ideas?

I've attached .config and the dmesg output.

Thanks

Allen

